<title>UK: Capita retreats after recent strong run.</title>
<headline>Capita retreats after recent strong run.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Capita Group Plc plummeted on Wednesday in a mark-down following recent sharp gains, dealers said.</p>
<p>The shares -- which rocketed to a record 830p on March 17, double its value just five months ago -- were down 42-1/2p at 732-1/2 by 1430 GMT in volume of 116,846 shares.</p>
<p>&quot;There have been a few sellers and the stock has been marked lower just to find a level,&quot; said one dealer, &quot;after all they have had a cracking run.&quot;</p>
<p>A three-for-one share split in Capita Group takes efffect on April 16.</p>
<p>-- David Holmes, London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
